research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38083, 'Students translate relational statements word-for-word into algebraic equations, resulting in reversed relationships.', 'Writing the equation ''6S = P'' for the statement ''There are six times as many students as professors''.', 'algebraic', 'Algebraic translation', 'Equation writing', 'other', 'undergraduate students and adults', 'ZDM_Attridge_2015_Increasing', 'Nina Attridge, Matthew Inglis', '2015', 'ZDM Mathematics Education', 'uncoded', 'secondary', '725', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_Attridge_2015_Increasing.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38084, 'Students associate the visual cue of parentheses directly with the ''shower'' (distributive) procedure, leading them to incorrectly apply the distributive law to expressions involving only multiplication.', 'When given the expression 3(5(x - 2)), a student suggests distributing the 3 to both the 5 and the (x - 2). Similarly, for 7(x - 3)(x - 2), students multiply the 7 by both binomial factors.', 'algebraic', 'Distributive law', 'Multiplication of multiple factors', 'mixed', '9th grade', 'ZDM_David_2014_How', 'Maria Manuela David, Vanessa Sena Tomaz, Maria Cristina Costa Ferreira', '2014', 'ZDM Mathematics Education', 'deficit', 'primary', '100, 101, 102', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_David_2014_How.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38085, 'Students view algebraic expressions involving operations operationally as unfinished processes rather than structurally as objects, preventing them from recognizing a binomial in parentheses as a single numeric factor.', 'Students struggle to see that (x - 2) in the expression 7(x - 3)(x - 2) acts as a single number because the subtraction cannot be completed.', 'algebraic', 'Algebraic expressions', 'Process-object duality', 'mixed', '9th grade', 'ZDM_David_2014_How', 'Maria Manuela David, Vanessa Sena Tomaz, Maria Cristina Costa Ferreira', '2014', 'ZDM Mathematics Education', 'deficit', 'secondary', '100, 103', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_David_2014_How.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38086, 'Students'' concept images of limits at interval endpoints conflict with the formal definition, leading them to incorrectly believe the function must not be defined at the endpoint or that reaching the limit violates injectivity.', 'Linda draws asymptotes at x=1 and x=-1 because she believes the function cannot be defined there if it tends to 2, and later draws points just below and above 2, falsely concluding an injective function cannot exist.', 'calculus', 'Limits and continuity', 'Limit at endpoints', 'student', 'university and PhD', 'ZDM_Antonini_2011_Generating', 'Samuele Antonini', '2011', 'ZDM Mathematics Education', 'uncoded', 'primary', '212, 214, 215', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_Antonini_2011_Generating.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38087, 'Students conflate their inability to construct or transform a visual representation of an object with the mathematical impossibility of the object''s existence.', 'Federica attempts to construct a twice-differentiable convex function with three zeros by joining two curves, fails to make the join differentiable, and consequently assumes and tries to prove that the function is mathematically impossible.', 'calculus', 'Proof and argumentation', 'Proof by contradiction', 'student', 'university and PhD', 'ZDM_Antonini_2011_Generating', 'Samuele Antonini', '2011', 'ZDM Mathematics Education', 'uncoded', 'primary', '213', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_Antonini_2011_Generating.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38088, 'Students and experts overgeneralize the properties of highly familiar prototypes, which prevents them from generating valid mathematical examples that fall outside those narrow properties.', 'Marisa, a PhD student, relies heavily on the sine function as a prototype for periodic functions and generates an invalid conjecture that any periodic function must have a minimum period because it must repeat itself in the same way.', 'calculus', 'Periodic functions', 'Minimum period', 'student', 'university and PhD', 'ZDM_Antonini_2011_Generating', 'Samuele Antonini', '2011', 'ZDM Mathematics Education', 'uncoded', 'primary', '215, 216', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_Antonini_2011_Generating.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38089, 'Students incorrectly determine the value of a point on a number line by counting the number of tick marks from zero, disregarding the distance or spacing between the tick marks.', 'When presented with a number line where not all integer tick marks are drawn, a student identifies the third tick mark after zero as 3, even though the spacing indicates a different value.', 'whole_number', 'Number line', 'Locating numbers', 'other', 'primary and middle school', 'ZDM_Teppo_2014_Visual', 'Anne Teppo, Marja van den Heuvel-Panhuizen', '2014', 'ZDM Mathematics Education', 'deficit', 'secondary', '49', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_Teppo_2014_Visual.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38090, 'When using an empty number line to calculate, students may draw jumps that represent correct arithmetic values but violate the spatial and numerical left-to-right order of the line.', 'To solve 544 + 296 as 544 + 300 - 4, a student draws a forward jump of +300 to 844, and then draws a forward jump of -4 to 840, incorrectly placing 840 to the right of 844.', 'whole_number', 'Addition and subtraction', 'Empty number line', 'other', 'primary and middle school', 'ZDM_Teppo_2014_Visual', 'Anne Teppo, Marja van den Heuvel-Panhuizen', '2014', 'ZDM Mathematics Education', 'deficit', 'primary', '54, 55', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_Teppo_2014_Visual.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38091, 'Teachers incorrectly assume that their expert understanding of a number line''s transparent mathematical representation will be self-evident to students, leading to ambiguous instructions.', 'Using a continuous arc or ''hop'' on a number line to represent counting-on, while instructing students to count spaces, not points, resulting in confusion over how to align the count with the tick marks.', 'whole_number', 'Number line', 'Addition', 'other', 'primary and middle school', 'ZDM_Teppo_2014_Visual', 'Anne Teppo, Marja van den Heuvel-Panhuizen', '2014', 'ZDM Mathematics Education', 'deficit', 'primary', '46, 49, 50', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_Teppo_2014_Visual.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38092, 'Students inappropriately overuse rules and intuitions based on natural numbers when reasoning about the magnitude and density of rational numbers.', 'Stating that there are no numbers in between 0.3 and 0.4, or taking significantly longer to correctly compare fractions that are incongruent with natural number features, such as 1/3 versus 1/4.', 'rational', 'Rational number conceptual knowledge', 'Size comparison and density', 'student', 'preschool to age 12', 'ZDM_McMullen_2015_Preschool', 'Jake McMullen, Minna M. Hannula-Sormunen, Erno Lehtinen', '2015', 'ZDM Mathematics Education', 'deficit', 'primary', '813, 814, 818', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_McMullen_2015_Preschool.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38093, 'Students fail to uniquely define independent variables when formulating an algebraic model, sometimes using the same variable to represent distances from two different reference points.', 'A student used the expression 40^2 + x^2 + 120^2 + x^2 where ''x'' was used simultaneously as the distance from corner A and from corner B.', 'algebraic', 'Algebraic modeling', 'Defining variables', 'student', '14-15 year old students, Year 9', 'ZDM_Galbraith_2006_Framework', 'Peter Galbraith, Gloria Stillman', '2006', 'ZDM', 'deficit', 'primary', '149', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_Galbraith_2006_Framework.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38094, 'Students inappropriately truncate linear models by ignoring the y-intercept, using only the slope (rate of change) to predict outcomes for large values.', 'Students constructed the model y = 15.5x + 21, but when calculating the required number of bungee bands for a 580cm drop, they simply divided 580 by 15.5, ignoring the +21 intercept.', 'algebraic', 'Linear models', 'y-intercept', 'student', '14-15 year old students, Year 9', 'ZDM_Galbraith_2006_Framework', 'Peter Galbraith, Gloria Stillman', '2006', 'ZDM', 'deficit', 'primary', '153, 154', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_Galbraith_2006_Framework.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38095, 'Students struggle to translate concatenated list formulas from a graphing calculator into a simplified two-variable algebraic function due to a lack of understanding of notational syntax.', 'A student''s final algebraic equation still contained ''L5'' in the place where ''x'' should be, failing to substitute the list name with the standard algebraic variable.', 'algebraic', 'Algebraic functions', 'Notational syntax', 'student', '14-15 year old students, Year 9', 'ZDM_Galbraith_2006_Framework', 'Peter Galbraith, Gloria Stillman', '2006', 'ZDM', 'deficit', 'primary', '149, 156, 157', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_Galbraith_2006_Framework.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38096, 'Students fail to perceive that real-world constraints can be relaxed to find optimal solutions, instead strictly adhering to established patterns.', 'When asked where to place a 19th station optimally to minimize running distance, students simply placed it 10 meters away from the first or last stations, adhering to the 10m interval pattern rather than calculating the absolute shortest path.', 'other', 'Mathematical modelling', 'Relaxing constraints', 'student', '14-15 year old students, Year 9', 'ZDM_Galbraith_2006_Framework', 'Peter Galbraith, Gloria Stillman', '2006', 'ZDM', 'deficit', 'primary', '150', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_Galbraith_2006_Framework.pdf')).
research_corpus_misconception_row(row(38097, 'Students fail to recognize the affordance of technology like function graphers to verify algebraic equations, incorrectly believing that joining points on a data plotter is equivalent.', 'Students thought verifying an algebraic model by graphing was superfluous because they had already joined points on a spreadsheet data plot, not realizing the graphing calculator could superimpose a function graph over points to check accuracy.', 'algebraic', 'Verifying algebraic models', 'Technological tools', 'student', '14-15 year old students, Year 9', 'ZDM_Galbraith_2006_Framework', 'Peter Galbraith, Gloria Stillman', '2006', 'ZDM', 'deficit', 'secondary', '149', 'pdfs/ZDM/ZDM_Galbraith_2006_Framework.pdf')).
